  "evaluationNote": "CV F1 is the mean over 10 stratified group folds of the 295 training records (also used for tuning). Test scores come from 79 held-out records (16 distinct profiles) never used for training or tuning.",
  "limitations": [
    "Only 132 of the 374 records are distinct profiles, and the held-out test set holds just 16 of them, so the test scores rest on very few different people.",
    "Stress level carries the tree models. Without it, cross-validated F1 falls from 0.973 to 0.845 for the Decision Tree and from 0.991 to 0.806 for the Random Forest, while Logistic Regression rises to 0.957.",
    "Class balance varies widely across the ten folds (6% to 87% short sleep), and the same folds were used for tuning, so CV scores may be optimistic.",
    "Short sleep here means under 7 hours, not poor sleep quality or a sleep disorder. Predictions show associations, not causes, and are not medical advice."
  ]
